  <h3>Chips Combobox in Error State</h3>
  <p>
    When a user enters text that is considered to be invalid, the Chips Combobox
    module can enter an error state. Developers can validate the text entry and
    trigger invalid/valid states as needed.
  </p>
  <p>
    To turn on the error state, add a class of
    <code>chips-combobox--error</code>
    to the outer element of the module. To turn off the error state,
    remove the class.
  </p>
  <p>
    In addition to the inclusion of the modifier to turn on the error state,
    there should also be an accompanying error message relevant to the reason
    for the error. Per
    <code>a11y</code>
    rules, color alone should not be used to indicate an error. For more
    information, please see the
    <a href=`${urls.components}/field/#field-error-state`>
      field error state docs
    </a>
    .
  </p>

